        content: 'Strong Consistency:\n• Reads always return latest write\n• Higher latency, lower availability\n• Use: Financial transactions\n\nEventual Consistency:\n• Reads may return stale data temporarily\n• Lower latency, higher availability\n• System converges to consistent state\n• Use: Social media feeds, product catalogs\n\nCausal Consistency:\n• Related operations seen in order\n• Unrelated operations may be out of order\n• Balance between strong and eventual',
        codeExample: '// Eventual consistency example\n// Write to primary\nawait primary.write({ userId: 1, balance: 100 });\n\n// Replicas may not have update yet\nconst balance = await replica.read(1); // Might return old value\n\n// After replication delay, all replicas consistent\nsetTimeout(async () => {\n  const balance = await replica.read(1); // Returns 100\n}, replicationDelay);',
