        content: 'L1 cache reference: 0.5 ns\nL2 cache reference: 7 ns\nMain memory reference: 100 ns\nSSD random read: 150 μs\nHDD seek: 10 ms\nSame datacenter round trip: 0.5 ms\nInternet: California to Netherlands: 150 ms\n\nKey insights:\n• Memory is 100x faster than SSD\n• SSD is 100x faster than HDD\n• Network within datacenter is fast\n• Cross-region is slow\n\nDesign implications: Cache aggressively, minimize network hops, keep data close to users.',
