        id: 'sdcs-file-storage',
        title: 'Distributed File Storage (Dropbox / Drive)',
        content: 'Requirements: upload/download files, sync across devices, share, history, large files (multi-GB).\n\nKey ideas:\n\nChunking:\n• Split file into fixed (4MB) or content-defined (rolling hash, Rabin) chunks\n• Each chunk hashed (SHA-256); the file is described by an ordered list of chunk hashes\n• Identical chunks across users/files are stored once — global deduplication\n• Used by Dropbox, IPFS, restic, borg\n\nDelta sync:\n• Client computes new chunks; only chunks not already on the server are uploaded\n• Tiny edit in a 1GB file = upload one chunk\n\nMetadata service:\n• Maps user → file → chunk list → versions\n• Strongly consistent (typically RDBMS)\n• Versions / revision history are just different chunk lists pointing to immutable chunks\n\nBlob storage:\n• Chunks live in S3/GCS/Azure Blob, keyed by content hash\n• Erasure-coded for durability (e.g., Reed-Solomon 10+4)\n\nSharing:\n• Capability tokens (signed URLs) for public sharing\n• ACL service for permissions; flatten to bitmask cache for fast checks\n\nClient sync:\n• Watch local FS events (FSEvents, inotify)\n• Three-way merge for conflict resolution (or last-write-wins for non-collaborative files)\n• Offline-first: queue changes, replay on reconnect',
